'\"
.TH "rbc::MARKER" 3tcl 0\&.5\&.0 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::MARKER - Commands in namespace rbc::MARKER
.SH "GRAPH MARKER MARKER COMMAND"
.PP
Commands in this namespace document graph markers\&.
.PP
MARKER is used below as a placeholder for:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
GRAPHINST marker
.fi
.RE
.PP
Markers are graph annotations\&. They are independent of graph elements and do not contribute to the calculation
of axis limits\&.
.PP
Rbc provides six marker types:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌─────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Type    │ Description                                    │
├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ bitmap  │ Displays a Tk bitmap                           │
│ image   │ Displays a Tk image                            │
│ line    │ Displays one or more connected line segments   │
│ polygon │ Displays a filled and/or outlined polygon      │
│ text    │ Displays text                                  │
│ window  │ Displays an embedded Tk window                 │
└─────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.PP
A marker is created by specifying its type:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g
\&.g marker create text -name label -coords {1\&.0 2\&.0} -text "Operating point"
\&.g marker create line -name limit -coords {0 5 10 5} -outline red
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unlike elements and pens, the marker name is not a positional argument of MARKER create\&. Use -name to
select an explicit name\&. If -name is omitted, Rbc generates a marker name\&.
.SH "MARKER COORDINATES"
.PP
Marker coordinates are graph coordinates and are mapped through the axes selected by -mapx and -mapy\&.
.PP
The number of coordinates depends on the marker type:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌─────────────┬─────────────────────────┐
│ Marker type │ Coordinates             │
├─────────────┼─────────────────────────┤
│ bitmap      │ One or two X-Y pairs    │
│ image       │ One or two X-Y pairs    │
│ line        │ Two or more X-Y pairs   │
│ polygon     │ Three or more X-Y pairs │
│ text        │ One X-Y pair            │
│ window      │ One X-Y pair            │
└─────────────┴─────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.PP
For bitmap and image markers, one X-Y pair specifies the marker position\&. Two pairs specify opposite corners
of a bounding rectangle\&. Bitmap markers are scaled to that rectangle\&. Photo images are likewise scaled to the
rectangle; other Tk image types are drawn at their natural size\&.
.PP
Coordinate values may be Tcl numeric expressions\&. Inf, +Inf, and -Inf select elastic axis bounds\&.
.PP
An empty -coords value leaves the marker without drawable coordinates\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -coords {-Inf Inf} -anchor nw -text "upper left"
.fi
.RE
.SH "DRAWING ORDER"
.PP
Markers have their own display order\&. MARKER before and MARKER after change the position of a marker in
that order\&.
.PP
By default markers are drawn over graph elements\&. The -under option changes whether an individual marker is
drawn below or above the element layer\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker configure region -under yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
The marker ordering operations affect ordering between markers; they do not replace the -under setting\&.
.SH "ELEMENT ASSOCIATION"
.PP
-element associates a marker with an element:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name note -element signal -coords {2 5} -text signal
.fi
.RE
.PP
The marker is displayed only while the associated element is displayed\&. An empty -element value removes the
association\&.
.SH "MARKER BINDINGS"
.PP
Markers participate in graph component bindings\&. Bindings are made with MARKER bind\&.
.PP
Every marker has its marker name as an implicit binding tag\&. Additional tags are selected with -bindtags\&.
.PP
The default binding tags depend on the marker type:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌─────────┬───────────────────┐
│ Type    │ Default -bindtags │
├─────────┼───────────────────┤
│ bitmap  │ Bitmap all        │
│ image   │ Image all         │
│ line    │ Line all          │
│ polygon │ Polygon all       │
│ text    │ Text all          │
│ window  │ Window all        │
└─────────┴───────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name note -coords {1 2} -text "click me" -bindtags {annotation all}
\&.g marker bind annotation <Button-1> {
    puts "annotation selected"
}
.fi
.RE
.SH "MARKER TYPES AND OPTIONS"
.PP
All marker types share the coordinate, visibility, axis-mapping, naming, binding, state, drawing-order, and
offset options described below\&. Each concrete marker type then adds its own drawing options\&.
.PP
MARKER cget and MARKER configure operate on the option table of the concrete marker being addressed\&. An
option valid for one marker type is not necessarily valid for another\&.
.SS "COMMON MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌───────────────────────┬───────────────┬────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                │ Database name │ Database class │ Description                                         │
├───────────────────────┼───────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -bindtags tagList     │ bindTags      │ BindTags       │ Specifies additional binding tags associated with   │
│                       │               │                │ the marker\&. The marker name is always an implicit   │
│                       │               │                │ binding tag\&. The default class tag depends on the   │
│                       │               │                │ marker type\&.                                        │
│ -coords coordList     │ coords        │ Coords         │ Specifies the graph coordinates of the marker\&. The  │
│                       │               │                │ required number of coordinates depends on the       │
│                       │               │                │ marker type\&. The default is empty\&.                  │
│ -element elementName  │ element       │ Element        │ Associates the marker with an element\&. The marker   │
│                       │               │                │ is displayed only while that element is displayed\&.  │
│                       │               │                │ An empty value removes the association\&.             │
│ -hide boolean         │ hide          │ Hide           │ Specifies whether the marker is hidden\&. The default │
│                       │               │                │ is no\&.                                              │
│ -mapx axisName        │ mapX          │ MapX           │ Specifies the X axis used to map marker coordinates\&.│
│                       │               │                │ The axis must exist and must be an X axis\&. The      │
│                       │               │                │ default is x\&.                                       │
│ -mapy axisName        │ mapY          │ MapY           │ Specifies the Y axis used to map marker coordinates\&.│
│                       │               │                │ The axis must exist and must be a Y axis\&. The       │
│                       │               │                │ default is y\&.                                       │
│ -name markerName      │ —             │ —              │ Specifies the marker name\&. During creation, an      │
│                       │               │                │ omitted name is generated automatically\&.            │
│                       │               │                │ Reconfiguring -name renames the marker; the new     │
│                       │               │                │ name must be non-empty, must not begin with -, and  │
│                       │               │                │ must not already belong to another marker\&.          │
│ -state state          │ state         │ State          │ Specifies the marker state: normal, active, or      │
│                       │               │                │ disabled\&. The default is normal\&.                    │
│ -under boolean        │ under         │ Under          │ Specifies whether the marker is drawn below graph   │
│                       │               │                │ elements rather than above them\&. The default is no\&. │
│ -xoffset distance     │ xOffset       │ XOffset        │ Adds a horizontal screen-coordinate offset after    │
│                       │               │                │ the marker has been mapped\&. The default is 0\&.       │
│ -yoffset distance     │ yOffset       │ YOffset        │ Adds a vertical screen-coordinate offset after the  │
│                       │               │                │ marker has been mapped\&. The default is 0\&.           │
└───────────────────────┴───────────────┴────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SS "BITMAP MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Bitmap markers display a Tk bitmap\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create bitmap -name bitmap1 -coords {1 2} -bitmap questhead
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, bitmap markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌──────────────────────┬───────────────┬────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option               │ Database name │ Database class │ Description                                         │
├──────────────────────┼───────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -anchor anchor       │ anchor        │ Anchor         │ Specifies how the bitmap is positioned relative to  │
│                      │               │                │ its reference coordinates\&. The default is center\&.   │
│ -background color    │ —             │ —              │ Specifies the bitmap background color\&. This is a    │
│                      │               │                │ synonym for -fill\&.                                  │
│ -bg color            │ —             │ —              │ Synonym for -background\&.                            │
│ -bitmap bitmap       │ bitmap        │ Bitmap         │ Specifies the Tk bitmap to display\&.                 │
│ -fill color          │ background    │ Background     │ Specifies the bitmap background color\&.              │
│ -foreground color    │ —             │ —              │ Specifies the bitmap foreground color\&. This is a    │
│                      │               │                │ synonym for -outline\&.                               │
│ -fg color            │ —             │ —              │ Synonym for -foreground\&.                            │
│ -mask bitmap         │ mask          │ Mask           │ Specifies an optional bitmap mask\&.                  │
│ -outline color       │ foreground    │ Foreground     │ Specifies the bitmap foreground color\&.              │
│ -rotate degrees      │ rotate        │ Rotate         │ Specifies the rotation angle in degrees\&. The        │
│                      │               │                │ default is 0\&.                                       │
└──────────────────────┴───────────────┴────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SS "IMAGE MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Image markers display a Tk image\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
image create photo icon -file icon\&.png
\&.g marker create image -name iconMarker -coords {1 2} -image icon
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, image markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌──────────────────┬───────────────┬────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option           │ Database name │ Database class │ Description                                         │
├──────────────────┼───────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -anchor anchor   │ anchor        │ Anchor         │ Specifies how the image is positioned relative to   │
│                  │               │                │ its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.              │
│ -image imageName │ image         │ Image          │ Specifies the Tk image to display\&.                  │
└──────────────────┴───────────────┴────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SS "LINE MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Line markers draw connected line segments through their X-Y coordinate pairs\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create line -name threshold -coords {-Inf 5 Inf 5} -outline red -linewidth 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, line markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌────────────────────────┬──────────────┬────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                 │ Database name│ Database class │ Description                                          │
├────────────────────────┼──────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -arrow position        │ arrow        │ Arrow          │ Specifies whether arrowheads are drawn at the ends   │
│                        │              │                │ of the line marker\&. Accepted values are none, first, │
│                        │              │                │ last, and both\&. The default is none\&.                 │
│ -arrowshape {a b c}    │ arrowShape   │ ArrowShape     │ Specifies the arrowhead geometry as three screen     │
│                        │              │                │ distances\&. a is the distance from the arrowhead      │
│                        │              │                │ neck to its tip, b is the distance from the trailing │
│                        │              │                │ points to the tip, and c is the distance from the    │
│                        │              │                │ line edge to the trailing points\&. The default is     │
│                        │              │                │ {8 10 3}\&.                                            │
│ -cap style             │ cap          │ Cap            │ Specifies the line cap style\&. Accepted styles are    │
│                        │              │                │ butt, projecting, and round\&. The default is butt\&.    │
│ -dashes dashList       │ dashes       │ Dashes         │ Specifies the dash pattern\&. An empty value selects   │
│                        │              │                │ a solid line\&.                                        │
│ -dashoffset distance   │ dashOffset   │ DashOffset     │ Specifies the offset into the dash pattern\&. The      │
│                        │              │                │ default is 0\&.                                        │
│ -fill color            │ fill         │ Fill           │ Specifies the color used for the off portions of a   │
│                        │              │                │ dashed line\&. An empty value uses ordinary on/off     │
│                        │              │                │ dashes\&. The default is empty\&.                        │
│ -join style            │ join         │ Join           │ Specifies how adjacent segments are joined\&.          │
│                        │              │                │ Accepted styles are bevel, miter, and round\&. The     │
│                        │              │                │ default is miter\&.                                    │
│ -linewidth distance    │ lineWidth    │ LineWidth      │ Specifies the line width\&. The default is 1\&.          │
│ -outline color         │ outline      │ Outline        │ Specifies the primary line color\&. Arrowheads use     │
│                        │              │                │ this color\&. The default is black\&.                    │
│ -xor boolean           │ xor          │ Xor            │ Specifies whether the line is drawn using XOR        │
│                        │              │                │ drawing\&. The default is no\&.                          │
└────────────────────────┴──────────────┴────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SH ARROWHEADS
.PP
Line markers may draw an arrowhead at either end of the line by using the -arrow option\&. Accepted values
are none, first, last, and both\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g
pack \&.g
\&.g marker create line -name direction -coords {0 0 5 4 10 2} -outline red -linewidth 2 -arrow last
.fi
.RE
.PP
The arrowhead shape may be adjusted with -arrowshape\&. It accepts three screen distances {a b c}:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker configure direction -arrow both -arrowshape {8 10 3}
.fi
.RE
.PP
a specifies the distance from the arrowhead neck to its tip, b specifies the distance from the trailing
points to the tip, and c specifies the distance from the outside edge of the line to the trailing points\&.
.PP
The arrowhead uses the line marker's -outline color\&. The line shaft is shortened to the neck of the
arrowhead so that it does not protrude through the filled arrowhead\&.
.PP
Screen-distance units accepted by Tk may also be used:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker configure direction -arrowshape {8p 10p 3p}
.fi
.RE
.SS "POLYGON MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Polygon markers draw the closed polygon formed by their coordinate pairs\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create polygon -name region -coords {0 0 4 0 4 3 0 3} -fill lightblue -outline navy
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, polygon markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌───────────────────────┬──────────────┬────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                │ Database name│ Database class │ Description                                        │
├───────────────────────┼──────────────┼────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -cap style            │ cap          │ Cap            │ Specifies the outline cap style\&. Accepted styles   │
│                       │              │                │ are butt, projecting, and round\&. The default is    │
│                       │              │                │ butt\&.                                              │
│ -dashes dashList      │ dashes       │ Dashes         │ Specifies the dash pattern used for the polygon    │
│                       │              │                │ outline\&. An empty value selects a solid outline\&.   │
│ -fill colorList       │ fill         │ Fill           │ Specifies the polygon fill colors\&. The value may   │
│                       │              │                │ contain one foreground color or a foreground and   │
│                       │              │                │ background color\&. With -stipple, the second color  │
│                       │              │                │ supplies the stipple background\&. An empty value    │
│                       │              │                │ disables filling\&. The default foreground color is  │
│                       │              │                │ red\&.                                               │
│ -join style           │ join         │ Join           │ Specifies how adjacent outline segments are        │
│                       │              │                │ joined\&. Accepted styles are bevel, miter, and      │
│                       │              │                │ round\&. The default is miter\&.                       │
│ -linewidth distance   │ lineWidth    │ LineWidth      │ Specifies the width of the polygon outline\&. The    │
│                       │              │                │ value must be non-negative\&. The default is 1\&.      │
│ -outline colorList    │ outline      │ Outline        │ Specifies the polygon outline colors\&. The value    │
│                       │              │                │ may contain one foreground color or a foreground   │
│                       │              │                │ and background color\&. For dashed outlines, the     │
│                       │              │                │ second color is used for the off portions of the   │
│                       │              │                │ dash pattern\&. An empty value disables the outline  │
│                       │              │                │ color\&. The default foreground color is black\&.      │
│ -stipple bitmap       │ stipple      │ Stipple        │ Specifies an optional stipple bitmap used when     │
│                       │              │                │ filling the polygon\&. An empty value selects an     │
│                       │              │                │ unstippled fill\&.                                   │
│ -xor boolean          │ xor          │ Xor            │ Specifies whether the polygon outline uses XOR     │
│                       │              │                │ drawing\&. The default is no\&.                        │
└───────────────────────┴──────────────┴────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SS "TEXT MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Text markers display one or more lines of text\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name annotation -coords {3 8} -text "maximum" -anchor s
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, text markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌──────────────────────┬───────────────┬──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option               │ Database name │ Database class       │ Description                                        │
├──────────────────────┼───────────────┼──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -anchor anchor       │ anchor        │ Anchor               │ Specifies how the text is positioned relative to   │
│                      │               │                      │ its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.             │
│ -background color    │ background    │ MarkerBackground     │ Specifies the text background color\&. This is a     │
│                      │               │                      │ synonym for -fill\&.                                 │
│ -bg color            │ —             │ —                    │ Synonym for -background\&.                           │
│ -fill color          │ —             │ —                    │ Specifies the text background color\&.               │
│ -font font           │ font          │ Font                 │ Specifies the font used to draw the text\&.          │
│ -foreground color    │ foreground    │ Foreground           │ Specifies the text color\&. This is a synonym for    │
│                      │               │                      │ -outline\&.                                          │
│ -fg color            │ —             │ —                    │ Synonym for -foreground\&.                           │
│ -justify justify     │ justify       │ Justify              │ Specifies justification of multiline text\&. The     │
│                      │               │                      │ default is left\&.                                   │
│ -outline color       │ —             │ —                    │ Specifies the text color\&. The default is black\&.    │
│ -padx padding        │ padX          │ PadX                 │ Specifies horizontal padding around the text\&. The  │
│                      │               │                      │ default is 4\&.                                      │
│ -pady padding        │ padY          │ PadY                 │ Specifies vertical padding around the text\&. The    │
│                      │               │                      │ default is 4\&.                                      │
│ -rotate degrees      │ rotate        │ Rotate               │ Specifies the text rotation angle in degrees\&. The  │
│                      │               │                      │ default is 0\&.                                      │
│ -shadow shadow       │ shadow        │ Shadow               │ Specifies the text shadow\&.                         │
│ -text text           │ text          │ Text                 │ Specifies the text to display\&.                     │
└──────────────────────┴───────────────┴──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SS "WINDOW MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Window markers display a Tk window inside the graph\&.
.PP
The window must be managed by the graph marker\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
button \&.g\&.info -text Info
\&.g marker create window -name infoMarker -coords {2 4} -window \&.g\&.info
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, window markers support:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌──────────────────┬───────────────┬────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option           │ Database name │ Database class │ Description                                        │
├──────────────────┼───────────────┼────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -anchor anchor   │ anchor        │ Anchor         │ Specifies how the window is positioned relative to │
│                  │               │                │ its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.             │
│ -height distance │ height        │ Height         │ Specifies an explicit positive height for the      │
│                  │               │                │ embedded window\&. When left at its initial default  │
│                  │               │                │ of 0, the child's requested height is used\&.        │
│                  │               │                │ Explicitly configuring 0 is not accepted\&.          │
│ -width distance  │ width         │ Width          │ Specifies an explicit positive width for the       │
│                  │               │                │ embedded window\&. When left at its initial default  │
│                  │               │                │ of 0, the child's requested width is used\&.         │
│                  │               │                │ Explicitly configuring 0 is not accepted\&.          │
│ -window pathName │ window        │ Window         │ Specifies the Tk window managed by the marker\&. The │
│                  │               │                │ window must be a direct child of the graph widget\&. │
│                  │               │                │ An empty value removes the managed window\&.         │
└──────────────────┴───────────────┴────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.SH "OPTION DATABASE"
.PP
Marker options may be supplied through Tk's option database\&. Each concrete marker type has its own resource
class:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌─────────────┬─────────────────┐
│ Marker type │ Resource class  │
├─────────────┼─────────────────┤
│ bitmap      │ BitmapMarker    │
│ image       │ ImageMarker     │
│ line        │ LineMarker      │
│ polygon     │ PolygonMarker   │
│ text        │ TextMarker      │
│ window      │ WindowMarker    │
└─────────────┴─────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.PP
The resource name is the marker name\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
option add *Graph\&.TextMarker\&.Foreground navy
option add *Graph\&.LineMarker\&.LineWidth 2
.fi
.RE


